1
00:00:00,435 --> 00:00:05,049
Two balls. Same height. Different weights. Which lands first in a vacuum?

2
00:00:07,435 --> 00:00:10,751
Meet Dekisugi-kun, a science companion you teach.

3
00:00:11,012 --> 00:00:14,699
You read the evidence, then explain the idea in your own words.

4
00:00:16,301 --> 00:00:17,925
First, make a prediction.

5
00:00:18,186 --> 00:00:22,475
Here, I think the heavier ball will fall faster. Let's check the evidence.

6
00:00:24,068 --> 00:00:28,752
The lesson explains both the principle and the conditions under which it holds.

7
00:00:29,013 --> 00:00:31,054
The next step is to teach it back.

8
00:00:32,668 --> 00:00:34,523
Now the material disappears.

9
00:00:34,784 --> 00:00:39,352
I explain that the balls fall together when air resistance is negligible.

10
00:00:39,613 --> 00:00:42,767
Typing is a full learning route, alongside voice.

11
00:00:44,368 --> 00:00:48,751
The app shows key-term coverage, then asks a fixed follow-up question.

12
00:00:49,012 --> 00:00:51,595
A wrong choice brings a hint and another

13
00:00:51,595 --> 00:00:54,438
try, so I can rethink the missing condition.

14
00:00:56,035 --> 00:00:59,222
The record shows which of the companion's misconceptions

15
00:00:59,222 --> 00:01:01,670
were corrected, and which are still unsure.

16
00:01:01,930 --> 00:01:04,017
The goal is a clearer explanation.

17
00:01:05,635 --> 00:01:09,461
Optional Plus adds companion styling and parent reports.

18
00:01:09,722 --> 00:01:12,797
This is a RevenueCat Test Store purchase, with

19
00:01:12,797 --> 00:01:16,006
no real charge. The core lessons stay available.

20
00:01:17,601 --> 00:01:19,619
Read it. Explain it. Rethink it.

21
00:01:19,880 --> 00:01:22,245
Dekisugi-kun. Learn by teaching.

